    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The issue is that the \"lighter, more generic retrieval model\" on the new architecture won't be able to process those datasets with the same level of semantic nuance. Without your specific indexing and the low-latency weight caching from the H-9 hardware, the retrieval accuracy for the complex historical documents will drop significantly. \n\nIs there a way to integrate your current processing logic into the new environment, or is the migration strictly limited to the raw data?",
